From 9d878c5d7625ecd5f4c3e9117c7d0bea4600c283 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: BellSoft <info@bell-sw.com>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 20:08:46 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(java): catalog the vendor's JDK and NIK runtimes with
 the osv-internal module

Local (vendor-specific) change, applied after the upstream series.

Add the java-vendor-jdk-cataloger, which identifies standalone vendor
runtimes with the shared github.com/bell-sw/osv-internal detector and
reports them with the identity of the prototype OSV ecosystems:

* JDK/JRE: package type VendorJdkPkg (the module's purl name), name =
  variant (jdk, jre, jdk-lite, ...), version in product notation
  (21.0.2+14, 8u402+7), purl
  pkg:generic/<namespace>/<jdk name>@<v>?package_type=<variant>, ecosystem
  "<JDK family>:<major>";
* Native Image Kit: package type VendorNikPkg, name = bundle (core,
  standard, full), version 23.1.0+1, purl
  pkg:generic/<namespace>/<nik name>@<v>?package_type=<bundle>, ecosystem
  "<NIK family>:<nik major>-<java major>" (the bundled Java version is kept
  in the JavaVMInstallation metadata).

Detection is anchored on the JVM library of Linux, macOS and Windows
layouts (libjvm.so, libjvm.dylib, jvm.dll; names compared
case-insensitively) with a release-file fallback; other vendors are never
reported. Runtimes under /usr/lib/jvm on the vendor distributions are apk
packages and are left to the apk ecosystem. The packages carry no CPE.

The module-free java-binary-vendor-jdk / java-binary-vendor-nik
classifiers of the upstream series are superseded and removed from the
default classifier set. The guards of the generic java classifiers and of
the JVM release cataloger now ask the module's detector
(vendorjdk.IsRuntimeHome), so the cataloger and the guards cannot disagree
about a runtime; jvmvendor only locates the runtime home. Both types are
excluded by file-ownership overlap.

The release type the module derives from a JDK version (psu, cpu, cspu) is
exposed as "vendor-release-type=<type>" in the buildInfo field of the JVM
release metadata.

The tests build their runtimes with the module's testfix package; no
fixture is kept on disk.

go.mod requires github.com/bell-sw/osv-internal v0.5.0 (private; the build
replaces the import path with the module source installed by the
osv-internal package, see the APKBUILD).
